          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिखवाना — dikhvānā — \"to have (something) looked at\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अरुण ने अपनी रिपोर्ट डाक्टर को दिखवाई। Aruṇ ne apnī riporṭ ḍākṭar ko dikhvāī. Arun had the doctor look at his report."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने आँख दिखवाई, usne ā̃kh dikhvāī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिखवाना (dikhvānā) is the second causative of dekhnā, \"to see\", which CDIAL lists under dṛkṣati, a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 6507): dikhānā is \"to show\", and dikhvānā is \"to have something seen to\", usually by a doctor."
            }
          ]
